            "review_title": "Review at Takumi II Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Reginald W\nDa Nang, Vietnam502 contributions\n0\nGood choice for Japanese food\nDec 2018 • Couples\nMy wife and I visited today and enjoyed a moderately priced lunch. She had chirashi-sushi and I had katsudon. In Japan, the chirashi would have rated a 2.5. Here, I give it 3.5. The fish was just okay—cut in pieces that were too little to really enjoy properly, but of okay quality. The rice was a little disappointing, too, but still alright. Miso soup, would rate a 3. My katsudon, however, was much better and would rate a 4 even in Japan, the rice being the only weak part of the meal. Here, I rate it a solid 5. The side dishes were not bad, especially the stewed beef tongue. Given that two of us had lunch sets that we enjoyed moderately and paid only a total of 330,000 VND (about $13.00 US) I feel there was little to complain about. Service was quite pleasant and efficient. Will certainly go back.\nRead more\nWritten December 22, 2018",
