            "review_title": "Review at Takumi II Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jeffrey D\nCalifornia23 contributions\n0\nGreat Japanese Outside the Old Quarter\nAug 2018\nI find most restaurants in Hanoi simply go through the motions in terms of food and service. Takumi (we tried the outlet on Linh Lang) rises above the ubiquitous culinary mediocrity. The menu is extensive, and offers most Japanese favorites. The real highlight is the excellent preparation of quality ingredients. While the sashimi, sushi, and rolls lean towards the expensive side, most dishes fall in the $5-8 dollar range. The cooking skill, flavors and complexity are superb. We tried the egglplant and tofu braise in rich dashi broth, fried prawns with sweet mayo, chicken wings, pork ribs with daikon, and two maki rolls. I was absolutely amazed to be presented with a small serving of yuzu kosho (grated yuzu citrus and green chili) along with the sushi. Very rare!!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 29, 2018",
